1.1.text:
Article 30

Women's Protection includes:
a. strengthening and development of women's protection service provider institutions;
b. prevention of violence against women; and
c. strengthening and development of service provider institutions for women victims of violence;

Article 35

1. The Agency is responsible for implementing efforts to prevent the occurrence of Violence against Women.
2. Prevention as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented in the form of:
a. conducting counseling and socialization regarding matters relating to violence against women;
b. conducting socialization on women's rights;
c. seeking to improve education for women;
d. providing counseling to immediately report to local authorities if Violence against women occurs;
e. empowering social community organizations and women's organizations to increase women's knowledge and insight; and
f. establishing a network in order to prevent violence against women.

Article 39

1. Facilitation of the establishment of service provider institutions as referred to in Article 36 paragraph (2) letter a shall be implemented by establishing family learning centers.
2. The stages of establishing family learning centers include:
a. preparing regulations;
b. preparing human resources;
c. preparing facilities and infrastructure; and
d. establishment of family learning centers.
3. Family learning centers function:
a. as service institutions in prevention and counseling;
b. as a referral liaison point as a solution for child and family problems;
c. strengthening family capacity in caring for and protecting children;
d. as a place for family learning through education for parents; and
e. as a holistic integrative family one-stop service based on children's rights.

Article 13

1. The Regional Government is responsible for preparing planning of policies, programs and development activities with a Gender perspective.
2. The responsibility as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be coordinated by the PD that administers governmental affairs in the field of development planning, research and Regional development.
3. The planning as referred to in paragraph (1) includes stages:
a. Musrenbangdus;
b. Musrembangdes/kel;
c. Musrembangcam;
d. Musrenbang at regional level;
e. preparation of RPJMD;
f. preparation of PD Renstra;
g. preparation of PD Renja; and
h. RKPD;
i. preparation of RAPBD;
4. The planning as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be carried out through Gender analysis using the Gender Analysis Pathway method or other analysis methods.
5. The implementation of Gender analysis on the RPJMD and PD Renstra may cooperate with Higher Education institutions or other parties who have capability in their field.

